===================================================================================================
[Load|Store] Multiple [Increment|Decrement] [After|Before]
===================================================================================================
LDMIA r1, {r2, r3, r4}
  r2 = r1[0]
  r3 = r1[4]
  r4 = r1[8]

   after instruction r1 = r1 + 4 * 3

STMIA  r1, {r2, r3}
   r1[0]  = r2
   r1[4]  = r3



===================================================================================================
[MCR|MRC] CoProcessor Registers   (Remember these travel LEFT)
http://www.heyrick.co.uk/assembler/coprocmnd.html#mrc
===================================================================================================
* These transfer control from ARM register to CoProcessor registers
* Using the travel left plan, MRC does C to R and MCR does R to C

* E.g., mcr  co-pro  op1  ARM-reg   copro-reg  copro-reg2  op2 
        mcr  p15     0    r0        c8         c3           1  // flush TLB by MVA 

Essentially 
<co-pro - copro-reg>    : select a Class of operation like cp15 - c8 is for TLB operations.

<op1, op2, copro-reg2>  : select the individual method within that class. So <0, 1, c3> selects flush by MVA


